mum operations to transform one string to another",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Edit Distance"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3515","Operations: insert, delete, substitute",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Edit Distance"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3559","Time complexity: where , are string lengths",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Edit Distance"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3637","Recurrence relation:",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Edit Distance"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3663","If :",["Classic Problems","Edit Distance","Recurrence relation:"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3722","Else:",["Classic Problems","Edit Distance","Recurrence relation:"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3796","Matrix Chain Multiplication",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3832","Problem: Find optimal parenthesization to minimize scalar multiplications",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Matrix Chain Multiplication"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3911","Time complexity: for the DP solution",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Matrix Chain Multiplication"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-3964","Space complexity: for the memoization table",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Matrix Chain Multiplication"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4024","Recurrence: for",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Classic Problems","Matrix Chain Multiplication"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4138","Algorithmic Patterns",["Dynamic Programming Reference"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4165","State Definition",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Algorithmic Patterns"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4265","State dimensions depend on problem constraints",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Algorithmic Patterns","State Definition"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4317","Example: LCS uses 2D state for string positions",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Algorithmic Patterns","State Definition"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4370","Common patterns:",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Algorithmic Patterns","State Definition"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4408","1D state (Fibonacci, climbing stairs)",["Dynamic Programming Reference"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4466","2D state (LCS, edit distance)",["Dynamic Programming Reference"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4519","3D state (complex constraints)",["Dynamic Programming Reference"]],["p-e1f9864d7420c718.html","source-block-4553","Transition Function",["Dynamic Programming Reference","3D state (complex constraints)"]]],"format_version":2}